SEQUENCE A: E[c₃] = C(n,3)/4 — Average 3-cycles
------------------------------------------------------------

  Each triple of vertices forms a 3-cycle with probability 2/8 = 1/4.
  (2 cyclic orientations out of 8 possible.)
  E[c₃] = C(n,3) × 1/4 = n(n-1)(n-2)/24

  n= 2: E[c₃] = 0 = 0.00
  n= 3: E[c₃] = 1/4 = 0.25
  n= 4: E[c₃] = 1 = 1.00
  n= 5: E[c₃] = 5/2 = 2.50
  n= 6: E[c₃] = 5 = 5.00
  n= 7: E[c₃] = 35/4 = 8.75
  n= 8: E[c₃] = 14 = 14.00
  n= 9: E[c₃] = 21 = 21.00
  n=10: E[c₃] = 30 = 30.00
  n=11: E[c₃] = 165/4 = 41.25
  n=12: E[c₃] = 55 = 55.00

  Numerator sequence: [0, 1, 1, 5, 5, 35, 14, 21, 30, 165, 55, 143, 91, 455, 140]
  Integer values at n ≡ 0,1 (mod 4): [0, 1, 5, 14, 21, 30, 55, 91, 140, 170, 204]


